>>> how to copy multi-line from clipboard to ollama in zsh shell
To copy multi-line text from the clipboard to Ollama in a Zsh shell, you can follow these steps:

1. Ensure your system has `xclip` installed for copying and pasting to/from the X11 clipboard.
2. If `xclip` is not installed, you can install it using your package manager. For example, on Ubuntu or Debian:
   ```
   sudo apt-get install xclip
   ```
   On Fedora:
   ```
   sudo dnf install xclip
   ```

3. Open the Ollama session where you want to paste the copied text.

4. To copy text from the clipboard into Ollama, use the following command in your Zsh shell:
   ```sh
   echo -n "Press Enter when ready to paste..." && read -s
   xclip -selection clipboard -o | tr -d '\r' | while IFS= read -r line; do ollama -a "$line"; done
   ```
   Explanation of the command:
   - `echo -n "Press Enter when ready to paste..." && read -s`: This prompts you to press Enter and waits for your input without echoing the 
Enter key. It is a simple way to wait for user confirmation.
   - `xclip -selection clipboard -o`: Retrieves the contents of the clipboard.
   - `tr -d '\r'`: Removes any Windows-style carriage returns (`\r`) from the clipboard content.
   - `while IFS= read -r line; do ollama -a "$line"; done`: Iterates over each line of the clipboard content and passes it to Oll^C

